course: dictionary
lesson: 9161
title: Snowball: a word that grows
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A snowball is a ball of snow pressed together with your hands. Snowball is also a verb: to snowball means to grow bigger and bigger, faster and faster, like a ball rolling through snow.
explain: The words around a word show you which meaning is used. «Children make snowballs and have snowball fights» is about a ball of snow. «They grew like a snowball rolling downhill» is about growing fast. Ask yourself: is the sentence describing something you can hold, or something getting bigger?
explain: Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it. «A small problem can snowball into a big one» means the problem grows quickly. Try it: "A small problem can grow bigger and bigger into a big one." It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: A snowball is a ball of snow pressed together with the hands.
fact: As a verb, «snowball» means to grow bigger and bigger, faster and faster.
fact: A snowball fight is a game where people throw snowballs at each other.
fact: The snowball effect is when a small problem grows into a big one.
fact: In Ukrainian, «snizhky» means snowballs or a snowball fight.
exercise: «On ice you walk carefully, and you never throw snowballs at faces.» Why should you never throw snowballs at faces? | *They can injure eyes | They melt too slowly | They are too heavy to lift | They make the ice colder
exercise: «They grew like a snowball rolling downhill, picking up land by war, by marriage and by deals.» What does snowball mean here? | To press snow into a hard ball | To melt slowly away | *To grow bigger and bigger, faster and faster | To throw snow at someone
exercise: In «hraimo v snizhky!», the children are about to play a game. What game is it? | Snowman building | *Snowball fight | Ice skating | Sledging
test: Which word means a ball of snow pressed together with the hands? | Icicle | Snowman | *Snowball | Snowflake
test: «A small problem can snowball into a big one.» What does snowball mean here? | *Grow bigger and bigger, faster and faster | Throw at someone | Melt away | Freeze solid
exam: Mia reads, «A comet is a dirty snowball that grows a glowing head and tails.» What does snowball mean here? | A ball of snow you can throw | A winter game with friends | *An icy lump of ice and dust in space | A snowman with a carrot nose
